{title: Daughter of Asher}
{subtitle: Genesis 46:17; Numbers 26:44–46; 1 Chronicles 7:30–31}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Am] | [Bb] |
| [F] [C] | [Dm] | [Am] | [Bb] [C] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Jacob's children gathered round
Asher stood [Am]among the sons
Imnah first [Bb]and Ishvah there
Ishvi named [F]in ancient lands
Be[A]riah walked [Dm]with them all
And his sister Ser[Am]ah too
Her name was kept [Bb]in holy text
Part of Jacob's house [F]of two
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The sons of [A]Asher [Dm]by their clans
From Imnah the Im[Am]nite line
From Ishvi the Is[Bb]hvite name
From Beriah the Beriite [F]shine
Serah was the daugh[Am]ter's [Dm]name
Recorded in the census [Am]plain
Seventy souls went down [Bb]to stay
In the land of Egypt's grain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Chron[F]icles tell [A]the fami[Dm]ly tree
Asher's sons are listed clear
[Am]Imnah Ishvah Ishvi and Beriah
[Bb]Serah stands beside them near
Heber [F]son of Beriah [A]too
[Dm]Malchiel his brother's name
Fa[Am]ther of Birzaith they say
[Bb]In the book of life's own frame
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The sons of [F]Asher by their [A]clans
[Dm]From Imnah the Imnite line
From [Am]Ishvi the Ishvite name
From [Bb]Beriah the Beriite shine
Ser[F]ah was the daughter's [A]name
[Dm]Recorded in the census plain
[Am]Seventy souls went down [Bb]to stay
In the land of Egypt's grain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Names [F]preserved in [A]holy [Dm]scroll
[Bb]Not forgotten [F]in the tale
[C]Daughter Serah [Dm]stands apart
[Bb]In the geneal[F]ogy's [C]veil
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Serah's [Dm]name is spoken still
[C6]In the [Bb]records old and [C][Dm]new
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
